  "content": {
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Introduction",
        "text": "Florence Jacqueline Sylvie Devouard ( née Nibart ; born 10 September 1968) is a French agricultural engineer who served as the chair of the Wikimedia Foundation board of trustees between October 2006 and July 2008."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Education",
        "text": "Devouard holds an engineering degree in agronomy from ENSAIA and a DEA in genetics and biotechnologies from INPL ."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Career",
        "text": "On 9 March 2008, Devouard was elected member of the municipal council of Malintrat .\nDevouard joined the board of trustees of the Wikimedia Foundation in June 2004 and became its chair in October 2006, succeeding Jimmy Wales . She has served on the Advisory Board of the Foundation since July 2008.\nCo-founder of Wikimedia France in October 2004, she was vice-chair of its board as of 2011 until December 2012."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Recognition",
        "text": "On 16 May 2008, she was made a knight in the French National Order of Merit , proposed by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs as \"chair of an international foundation\"."
      },
      {
        "heading": "See also",
        "text": "France portal Biography portal\nList of Wikipedia people"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Further reading",
        "text": "Lih, Andrew . The Wikipedia Revolution: How a Bunch of Nobodies Created the World's Greatest Encyclopedia . Hyperion , New York City . 2009. First Edition. ISBN 978-1-4013-0371-6 (alkaline paper)."
      },
      {
        "heading": "External links",
        "text": "Bravitude and Chair of the Wikimedia Foundation on the main French TV network Wikinews interviews Florence Devouard, chair of the Wikimedia Foundation\nAnthere Consulting website Archived 23 February 2011 at the Wayback Machine Personal blog Wikimedia Foundation and sustainability User page on Wikipedia 2005 Board candidacy presentation Video-Interview on 10 February 2007 at the Lift07 conference in Geneva \"What the future holds for Wikipedia\" . Swissinfo . 25 January 2008. Archived from the original on 6 October 2008 . Retrieved 26 January 2008 . Interview with Florence Devouard. 'Madame Wikipedia' runs web giant from village HQ Archived 21 October 2012 at the Wayback Machine 2007 AFP article A Life in the Day: Florence Devouard 2007 Times article"
